nk it's possible we'll see more  rules on masks and more strict  enforcement of mask wearing  i think there'll be targeted  interventions where he targets  geographical groups  and targets particular types of behavior  that are known to be infection drivers  there's a cobra meeting tomorrow they're  going to decide this there's probably  going to be more public education  one of the infection drivers in the uk  has been late night drinking  so i'm pretty sure that tomorrow we're  going to see a 10  p.m curfew on pups pubs will be closed  at 10 p.m  the risk there of course is people will  go in from the pub and carry on drinking  at home  we couldn't see further instructions on  the on the hospitality  industry as well i don't think schools  and universities are going to be  affected yet  where are we going uh dr campbell i mean  we've got winter  just around the corner you know for the  uk for the united states as well as  for us here in germany what does that  mean  does it mean in your opinion that we've  got  harder times coming for us  the simple answer to that brett is  absolutely yes we know that all  respiratory viruses spread more in the  winter  and people get cold noses so their  infection is reduced  people go inside and shut the window so  there's more  viral load in the air people don't go  out and get as much sunshine so there's  less vitamin  d circulating in the blood and all these  things can contribute towards spread of  infection  there's also the possibility of  influenza although we've got a very  active influenza program going at the  moment  but the next six months are going to be  critical the chief medical officer that  today said we've turned a corner  and really we've got a fork in the road  now we can decide which way to go  one way is that we could have this  exponential rise with cases doubling  the other way is we can get on top of  this virus and keep it managed over  winter  but whatever happens we are going to  have to be taking  a